<PublicLayout title="Privacy in this review" description="A factual description of the current guest and browser storage boundary."><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Local project storage</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">Project manifests, edits, checkpoints and saved resource collections use browser storage on this origin. Export your project to retain a portable copy. Clearing browser site data removes local records.</p></section><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Credentials</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">Core browsing, composition, editing and export need no provider key. BYO provider credentials must remain ephemeral and are never written to project manifests, D1 or R2.</p></section><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Hosting</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">ChatGPT Sites serves the site and receives ordinary page and asset requests. Review the hosting provider privacy policy for its processing. Tessellate does not add third-party analytics, advertise fabricated usage counts or provision an additional database for this review.</p></section><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Public previews</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">Resource previews use sandboxed frames without same-origin privileges. Treat all example content as synthetic demonstration data, not real employee records.</p></section><p class="flex flex-wrap gap-5"><a class="underline" href="https://github.com/danishgm-sketch/Tessellate">Repository and contributions</a><a class="underline" href="/docs">Documentation</a><a class="underline" href="/explore">Inspect resource licences</a></p></PublicLayout>
